        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/{size}/1922_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-02-09T05:37:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Trajector\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/48/1914_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Trajector:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I thought Christopher actually mentioned the Contract by name. It wasn't the first time he talked about the sleazy white-suit guy, and it was kind of offhand, but there was something about how he said \"when she took the contract on Slim.\" Maybe he said \"when the Contract talked to her about Slim\" or some similar phrasing.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>EDIT: At first I was confused, and you thought The Contract was named Slim. (Slim is the name of Mr. Fixer, as you know.)</p>\n<p>Yes, I thought they made it pretty obvious, but perhaps not by saying it explicitly. They like that kind of wordplay.</p>",
